1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,685
An A C I fabric upgrade is a weekend

2
00:00:03,685 --> 00:00:05,066
you do not get back.

3
00:00:05,066 --> 00:00:08,517
Two hundred switches, a cluster that must be fully

4
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:11,900
fit before anything moves, and one bad group away

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,109
from rebooting both v P C peers.

6
00:00:14,859 --> 00:00:17,875
What if Claude read the validator output,

7
00:00:17,875 --> 00:00:21,553
drafted the upgrade plan and explained every step,

8
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:25,231
while deterministic code did the work and a person

9
00:00:25,231 --> 00:00:28,468
approved every window? That is A C I upgrade

10
00:00:28,468 --> 00:00:30,748
automation, done the Cisco way.

11
00:00:31,498 --> 00:00:37,348
Gennoor Tech presents Cisco ACI Upgrade Automation with Claude.

12
00:00:38,098 --> 00:00:40,899
One fabric in. One upgraded fabric out,

13
00:00:40,899 --> 00:00:45,065
with every Cisco recommended check completed and recorded.

14
00:00:45,065 --> 00:00:48,441
You build the workflow in ten hands-on modules,

15
00:00:48,441 --> 00:00:51,673
and each one is something you can run against

16
00:00:51,673 --> 00:00:54,474
the lab fabric, review and demonstrate.

17
00:00:54,474 --> 00:00:56,916
Claude plans, drafts and explains.

18
00:00:56,916 --> 00:01:01,369
Python and Ansible execute. A human approves the consequential

19
00:01:01,369 --> 00:01:03,524
actions. Everything is logged.

20
00:01:04,274 --> 00:01:06,621
You start with the process itself,

21
00:01:06,621 --> 00:01:09,934
as Cisco documents it. Target release selection,

22
00:01:09,934 --> 00:01:12,902
the release notes and compatibility matrix,

23
00:01:12,902 --> 00:01:14,420
A P I C cluster first,

24
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,836
then switch groups, and why a v P C

25
00:01:16,836 --> 00:01:19,459
pair must never sit in the same group.

26
00:01:19,459 --> 00:01:21,391
Then you set up Claude Code,

27
00:01:21,391 --> 00:01:23,531
the Claude Agent S D K and an M

28
00:01:23,531 --> 00:01:26,223
C P server that exposes read-only A P I

29
00:01:26,223 --> 00:01:27,534
C queries as tools.

30
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:31,540
Then discovery. A Python client for the A P

31
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:32,827
I C R E S T A P I

32
00:01:32,827 --> 00:01:35,174
that logs in, pulls every node,

33
00:01:35,174 --> 00:01:39,792
controller, firmware version, cluster state and health score,

34
00:01:39,792 --> 00:01:41,760
and returns typed J S O N.

35
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:46,227
You run the Cisco pre-upgrade validator and the open-source

36
00:01:46,227 --> 00:01:49,028
validation script, parse the results,

37
00:01:49,028 --> 00:01:53,116
and let Claude explain each failure in plain language,

38
00:01:53,116 --> 00:01:56,144
citing the exact query that produced it.

39
00:01:56,894 --> 00:01:58,994
On day two the plan takes shape.

40
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:02,274
Claude proposes upgrade groups from the inventory,

41
00:02:02,274 --> 00:02:03,849
keeps v P C peers apart,

42
00:02:03,849 --> 00:02:06,277
orders the A P I C cluster before the

43
00:02:06,277 --> 00:02:09,163
leaves and spines, and maps every group to a

44
00:02:09,163 --> 00:02:12,444
maintenance window. The output is structured J S O

45
00:02:12,444 --> 00:02:14,412
N, validated against a schema,

46
00:02:14,412 --> 00:02:17,365
so a bad plan is rejected before anyone reads

47
00:02:17,365 --> 00:02:20,383
it. You then stage firmware in the repository,

48
00:02:20,383 --> 00:02:23,073
take a configuration export and snapshot,

49
00:02:23,073 --> 00:02:26,616
and raise the change request in ServiceNow through the

50
00:02:26,616 --> 00:02:27,403
Table A P I.

51
00:02:28,153 --> 00:02:31,537
Guardrails come next, and they are specific to this

52
00:02:31,537 --> 00:02:34,191
workflow. The agent can read the fabric,

53
00:02:34,191 --> 00:02:36,380
but it cannot trigger an upgrade.

54
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:40,162
Every maintenance policy and firmware group is created by

55
00:02:40,162 --> 00:02:43,811
deterministic code, after a person approves the plan in

56
00:02:43,811 --> 00:02:47,526
a GitHub pull request. Scheduled start times are checked

57
00:02:47,526 --> 00:02:51,706
against the approved window, an incomplete validator run blocks

58
00:02:51,706 --> 00:02:53,962
the next step, and every decision,

59
00:02:53,962 --> 00:02:56,284
prompt and A P I call is written to

60
00:02:56,284 --> 00:02:58,871
an audit log you can hand to the change

61
00:02:58,871 --> 00:02:59,269
board.

62
00:03:00,019 --> 00:03:03,216
Day three is execution. The runner upgrades the A

63
00:03:03,216 --> 00:03:05,761
P I C cluster, waits for the cluster to

64
00:03:05,761 --> 00:03:09,023
be fully fit, then moves through the switch groups

65
00:03:09,023 --> 00:03:12,154
one at a time, polling firmware status and never

66
00:03:12,154 --> 00:03:15,090
starting the next group until the last one is

67
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:17,570
healthy. If a node does not come back,

68
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:20,832
the run pauses and Claude writes the status update

69
00:03:20,832 --> 00:03:22,463
for the on-call engineer.

70
00:03:23,213 --> 00:03:27,091
Then verification. Pre and post snapshots of versions,

71
00:03:27,091 --> 00:03:30,466
faults, endpoint counts, routes and v P C state

72
00:03:30,466 --> 00:03:33,841
are compared by code, and Claude turns the diff

73
00:03:33,841 --> 00:03:36,641
into a readable report with a clear go,

74
00:03:36,641 --> 00:03:40,376
hold or roll back recommendation that a person signs

75
00:03:40,376 --> 00:03:40,663
off.

76
00:03:41,413 --> 00:03:44,684
Execution labs run on a small physical lab fabric

77
00:03:44,684 --> 00:03:47,421
with fictional hostnames, three A P I Cs,

78
00:03:47,421 --> 00:03:49,223
four leaves and two spines,

79
00:03:49,223 --> 00:03:52,627
so the cluster and switch groups really upgrade and

80
00:03:52,627 --> 00:03:56,499
reboot. The runner's failure paths are exercised against a

81
00:03:56,499 --> 00:03:59,103
mocked A P I C with recorded responses.

82
00:03:59,103 --> 00:04:01,973
You will fail a validator check on purpose,

83
00:04:01,973 --> 00:04:04,643
watch the pipeline block, fix the fault,

84
00:04:04,643 --> 00:04:07,380
and finish an end to end upgrade with the

85
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,782
full evidence bundle.

